# Nothing listed here is part of the customer-facing site. netlify.toml sets
# publish = "." — Netlify serves the repository as-is, with no build step — so
# the developer files sitting beside index.html would otherwise be fetchable on
# the live domain. DEPLOY.md in particular names the GitHub repository and every
# environment variable the save function needs.
#
# 404! forces the rule even when the file exists. There is no 404.html, so
# Netlify serves its own not-found page, which is the intent.
#
# A splat only matches at the end of a path on Netlify, so "/*.md" would not
# work — the five root documents are listed one by one.
/tests/*           /404.html  404!
/tools/*           /404.html  404!
/supabase/*        /404.html  404!
/CLAUDE.md         /404.html  404!
/DEPLOY.md         /404.html  404!
/EDITING-GUIDE.md  /404.html  404!
/IMAGES.md         /404.html  404!
/README.md         /404.html  404!
/package.json      /404.html  404!
/deno.lock         /404.html  404!
